A||N||7||jlruiz67||V8 HOW HARD??||||1||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||06-15-2000||04:04 AM||||Hello all<BR>I just finished working with a friend droping his damaged 2.8 and replacing it with a stock 2.8 fiero engine. Now my question is. How much harder is it to instal V8 Arche's V8 kit and engine than installing the stock? I know that there would be more work, but how dificult could it be? I have reaserch the conversion and I like to know if there is any mayor differences in the engine install. I finally selected V8 Archie as the supplier of the kit and plan to do the conversion after I feel more confident in the install. <P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan86gt3.8||06-15-2000||12:27 PM||||Well if you do archies kit you will have to cut some holes in your wheel well to stick the main pulleys through into the wheel well.  I think (am not sure thought that you might need to weld or modify the subframe some.  If you go with fuel injection you will need to work out a wiring harness for it and the computer.  I would also suspect some work to the fuel system.  There will also be a custom exhaust system that needs to be fabricated.   Theese are just some of the things to expect.  If you go to archies site he detials what all needs to be done and even has pics of some of it.  Hope this helps!||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||06-15-2000||02:28 PM||||One of V8 Archie's main selling point is that there is no welding or frame modification. There is a hole needed to be cut in the inner fender well, but it's a non-supporting panel, so you don't lose any strength or frame integrity. Still, it's more involved than a regular engine change over, mainly more time consuming rather than all that much harder, if you have the kit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||06-15-2000||02:59 PM||||The pulley sticks into the wheel well only on the LT1 the LS1 has a cam driven waterpump so no pulleys in the wheel well.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spyder||06-15-2000||10:40 PM||||The install isn’t that bad, I was financially challenged during my install so it took me awhile.  If you have the time and everything needed for the install it won’t take long at all.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||06-15-2000||10:46 PM||||I almost forgot,<BR>I used V8 Archie's master build kit.||||reg||1
Z||000006||pherder||06-16-2000||01:54 PM||||Orief, guys,<P>The pulley in the wheelwell only is used in the 92 or older Chevy SB.  The LT1 has a cam driven waterpump and the entire engine/transaxle has to be moved over ~2" so that the waterpump fits inside the frame, even Archie does this!  and he supplies different length axles for that swap.<P>Since noone has a LS1 installed and running that I know of (Archie's is almost done IAW a post of his to the Technet) I can't comment on the LS1 engine in a Fiero.<P>Paul<BR>88 Formula to get a 350 TPI to be drag raced and autocrossed.  Got the kit, got the TPI (three different types ... stock, large tube SLP system and a SuperRam), got the engine, got the transaxles (4 ... two Isuzus and 2 Getrags), wiring, PROM, clutch, etc.<P>Just need the time to finish the other two Fieros before starting this one....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dan86gt3.8||06-16-2000||05:01 PM||||So you have how man v8 fieros???  Man watch out fot the super ram car its gona be fast.  Is it a T.P.S ram?  my friend has one of thiers on his iroc and its really fast!||||reg||1
